@title EPISODE 07 • THE RELAY CARD
@bg track_stadium_day
@show suki
Relay cards go up at noon. Suki's name is on the 4x400. So is a sticky note on her locker in Cassie's bubbly handwriting: "not saying ANYTHING 🤐 but u should tell him before somebody else does. love u — C"
Suki: Cassie KNOWS. She swears she won't tell, but she's Cassie. It's gonna slip. She's gonna sneeze and it's gonna come out. Jayden and Paris and the whole team and I'm gonna be "the girl who."
> [Bold] "Then we tell them first. On our terms." -> a1
> [Bad] "Skip the relay. Lay low till it blows over." -> a2
> [Sweet] "Whatever happens, you have me." -> a3
> [Bitchy] "I'll make sure Cassie keeps her mouth shut." -> a4
*a1
@add Suki_Friendship 2
@add Suki_Truth 1
Suki: (shaking) Okay. Okay. After practice. You stand next to me.
@jump a_done
*a2
@add Suki_Friendship -1
@add Cassie_Threat 2
Suki fakes a limp at warmups. Cassie runs her leg and keeps looking back at Suki, worried. Nobody believes the limp, least of all Holloway.
@jump a_done
*a3
@add Suki_Friendship 3
Suki hugs you so hard your sunglasses fall off. You let them.
@jump a_done
*a4
@add Cassie_Threat -1
@add Team_Reputation -1
@show cassie
London: Cassie. A word.
Cassie: I KNOW. I haven't said anything! I've been eating my feelings. I had four churros at my mom's restaurant last night.
London: Just... keep holding it. A little longer.
Cassie: For Suki. Not for you. You're mean.
London: Correct.
*a_done
@if Suki_Truth 1 told
@bg locker_room
@show jayden
Jayden: Suki's been dodging me all week. Is she okay? You'd tell me.
London looks at the kindest guy on the team and lies straight to his face. Behind him, Jamal won't meet her eyes. "She's fine. Midterms."
@jump end
*told
@bg bleachers_evening
@show jayden
Suki tells him. All of it. Jayden doesn't yell. He just walks to the end of the bleachers and sits alone in the cold.
Jayden: (much later, to London) Thank you for not letting her hide it. Honestly? I think we've both been pretending for months.
He says it looking at the penthouse lights across campus. At Paris's window.
*end
